From e7997814937c3331a5e52ad309990fcbc40b628c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:15:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Linear solvers: descriptions, factory of preconditioners,
 modules

Each linear solver and each preconditioner is registered with a
description (LinearSolverDescription): library, kind (iterative, direct,
approximate solver or preconditioner), location of the computations,
accepted preconditioners, options and a short text.

- The preconditioners are registered in a new factory
  (PreconditionerFactory), which replaces the chain of tests on the name
  of the preconditioner. The factories list their entries (getNames) and
  give their descriptions (getDescription).
- The location of a linear solver or of a preconditioner is checked
  against the execution settings from its description, instead of being
  deduced from its name. The placements of the existing entries are
  unchanged. A linear solver registered without description computes
  where the device of MFEM computes and accepts any preconditioner.
- A preconditioner given to a linear solver which accepts none is
  refused, as is a preconditioner of another library given to a linear
  solver which only accepts the ones of its library (the Krylov solvers
  of hypre), with a message.
- The solvers and preconditioners of each library are registered by a
  module: MFEM and mfem-mgis (MFEMLinearSolvers.cxx), hypre
  (HypreLinearSolvers.cxx), MUMPS, cuDSS and AmgX in their files. The
  code is moved without change of behaviour.
- The linear solvers of the other libraries report their convergence
  through the LinearSolverConvergenceReport interface (AmgX, cuDSS):
  hasConverged and getNumberOfIterationsAtConvergence no longer depend
  on these libraries.
- The messages for an unknown solver or preconditioner name the missing
  optional library, or say that the entry is only available in
  parallel.
